From: Rick Carback <rick.carback@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/adreno: Skip the zap shader when the kernel runs at EL2

With the kernel at EL2 there is no hypervisor to place the PAS metadata
in an SHM bridge or to bridge the image region before auth-and-reset, so
a zap shader cannot be authenticated. The SECVID registers are
accessible to the kernel in that case, so leave secure mode directly
instead, as the a8xx path already does when the device tree carries no
zap-shader node, and drop the warning that assumes a broken DT.

On the ASUS Ascent QN10 (Glymur, Adreno X2-85) TrustZone does accept the
signed zap image once the metadata comes from TZMem, but the SoC resets
as soon as the CP runs CP_SET_SECURE_MODE. This matches
Akhil P Oommen's proposed "drm/msm/a6xx: Skip gpu secure fw load in EL2
mode" (never merged).
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a8xx_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a8xx_gpu.c
index f892731cd..6261de8d4 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a8xx_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a8xx_gpu.c
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 #include "a6xx_gpu.h"
 #include "a6xx_gmu.xml.h"
 
+#include <asm/virt.h>
 #include <linux/bitfield.h>
 #include <linux/devfreq.h>
 #include <linux/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.h>
@@ -801,7 +802,16 @@ static int hw_init(struct msm_gpu *gpu)
 	 * guessed wrong then access to the RBBM_SECVID_TRUST_CNTL register will
 	 * be blocked and a permissions violation will soon follow.
 	 */
-	ret = a6xx_zap_shader_init(gpu);
+	/*
+	 * With the kernel at EL2 there is no hypervisor to bridge the image
+	 * region for TrustZone, so a zap shader cannot be authenticated; the
+	 * SECVID registers are accessible to us instead. Leave secure mode
+	 * directly and ignore any zap-shader node.
+	 */
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ARM64) && is_kernel_in_hyp_mode())
+		ret = -ENODEV;
+	else
+		ret = a6xx_zap_shader_init(gpu);
 	if (!ret) {
 		OUT_PKT7(gpu->rb[0], CP_SET_SECURE_MODE, 1);
 		OUT_RING(gpu->rb[0], 0x00000000);
@@ -816,8 +826,9 @@ static int hw_init(struct msm_gpu *gpu)
 		 * have a debug UART to realize the error of their ways...
 		 * if you mess this up you are about to crash horribly)
 		 */
-		dev_warn_once(gpu->dev->dev,
-			"Zap shader not enabled - using SECVID_TRUST_CNTL instead\n");
+		if (!(IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ARM64) && is_kernel_in_hyp_mode()))
+			dev_warn_once(gpu->dev->dev,
+				"Zap shader not enabled - using SECVID_TRUST_CNTL instead\n");
 		gpu_write(gpu, REG_A6XX_RBBM_SECVID_TRUST_CNTL, 0x0);
 		ret = 0;
 	} else {
